     1	# F0021 — Native React semantic shell + OIDC/session contract and safe re-auth behavior
     2	
     3	**Feature ID:** F0021
     4	**Phase:** MVP — v0.1B
     5	**Status:** Planned — Phase A approved 2026-11-27 (plan run `2026-11-27-6cda122a`); Phase B approved 2026-11-27 (`approve-phase-b`)
     6	**Owner:** Product Manager (Phase A); Architect (Phase B)
     7	**Governing ADRs:** [ADR-0036](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0036-nebula-keeps-a-native-semantic-ux-onyx-is-a-reference-implementation.md) (Accepted), [ADR-0049](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0049-shared-identity-and-verified-principal-boundary.md) (Accepted for the F0001-S0006 boundary), [ADR-0051](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0051-browser-session-and-revocation-contract.md) (Proposed; decision recorded 2026-11-08; this feature is its proving feature), [ADR-0072](../../architecture/decisions/ADR-0072-observatory-is-a-read-only-projection.md) (Proposed; carry-in seam only)
     8	
     9	## Feature Statement
    10	
    11	**As an** insurance knowledge worker or reviewer
    12	**I want** to sign in once to a native Nebula web application that keeps my session on the server, renews it safely and never replays my decisions behind my back
    13	**So that** I can work in Nebula's semantic views without tokens in my browser, without losing work when a session expires, and without an action being submitted that I did not confirm.
    14	
    15	## Business Objective
    16	
    17	- **Goal:** deliver the first user-facing surface (master blueprint §3, §120.5): a same-origin backend-for-frontend (BFF) session, the React shell every later screen mounts into, and the re-authentication behavior that keeps reviewer decisions safe.
    18	- **Metric:** master blueprint §121.2 items 8 (session transport) and 9 (mutation continuity) pass against the real authentik issuance, storage, renewal and logout flow, including an upstream revocation failure. These are ADR-0051's formal acceptance conditions.
    19	- **Baseline:** today the proof-scope Review Panel (F0001-S0004) takes a bearer token from the URL or a text field. No session, renewal, logout, CSRF protection or shell exists.
    20	- **Target:** zero access or refresh tokens in any browser-readable storage, URL, or response body; exactly one upstream refresh per renewal burst; zero automatically replayed mutations; bounded `authentication_event` growth under a rejected-credential burst.
    21	
    22	## Problem Statement
    23	
    24	- **Current State:** the only UI is a proof page that asks for a raw bearer token. The CRM reference mixes an HttpOnly-cookie model with browser-direct renewal that writes tokens to `sessionStorage`, and its logout revokes a refresh token the browser never set (§119.3). Since F0002, every rejected credential writes one durable `authentication_event` row with no edge throttle (F0002 security review, medium).
    25	- **Desired State:** one BFF session model (ADR-0051 D1–D6), an application shell with app-wide routing, server-state caching, state and styling choices that F0022, F0023 and F0067 inherit, and re-authentication that preserves in-memory work and requires explicit re-confirmation of any blocked mutation.
    26	- **Impact:** F0022 (native review round trip) and F0023 (Entity 360) cannot ship a user-facing screen without this feature. ADR-0051 cannot be accepted without its proof.
    27	
    28	## Scope & Boundaries
    29	
    30	**In Scope:**
    31	- Sign-in through a same-origin BFF using the OIDC authorization-code flow with PKCE, state and nonce against authentik; an opaque `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, `SameSite` session cookie; server-held access and refresh tokens (S0001).
    32	- Cookie-authenticated calls to the existing engine routes with CSRF and origin checks on every state-changing request, and distinct unauthenticated / session-expired / denied / not-found outcomes (S0002).
    33	- A single coalesced server-side renewal path, refresh-token rotation, and server-enforced idle (30 min) and absolute (8 h) session bounds (S0003; operator decision D1).
    34	- Re-authentication in a popup that keeps the page's in-memory work, shows a blocked mutation as not submitted and requires explicit re-confirmation; a redirect fallback that restores only a sanitized route (S0004; D3).
    35	- Logout that revokes the server-held refresh token upstream, ends the server session and reports an upstream failure; cache and in-flight-work clearing on logout, principal change, active knowledge-base switch and grant-revision change (S0005).
    36	- The shell: signed-in home with the principal's display name and current tenant/knowledge-base memberships, an active knowledge-base selector that only narrows, and denied / not-found / signed-out / error screens (S0006; D2).
    37	- The route-level feature-flag and lazy-loading seam F0067 needs, and the existing proof Review Panel rehosted behind the session with the token-in-URL entry removed (S0007; D2).
    38	- Throttling of rejected credentials on both the bearer API and the BFF cookie path: 20 per client per 60 s, then `429` (S0008; D4; F0002 carry-in).
    39	- The §121.2 items 8 and 9 proof against real authentik, PostgreSQL and the rehosted Review Panel decision submission (S0009).
    40	
    41	**Out of Scope:**
    42	- Document 360, the full review batch workflow, renderer changes and reviewer-authority rules (F0022). The rehosted panel keeps its current F0001-S0004 behavior.
    43	- Entity 360 (F0023), search, chat and graph views (v0.2), and the Graph Observatory itself (F0067; only the seam is delivered).
    44	- New authorization grants, roles, resources or policy rows. The shell reads the principal's existing memberships; the engine stays the authorization boundary.
    45	- Retention of `authentication_event` rows (F0026) and production host, TLS termination and ingress choices (F0026, §117.1 item 3).
    46	- An idempotent command protocol for controlled mutation retry (§120.5 names it as later work).
    47	- External users (brokers, MGAs), self-registration, account linking and IdP migration (§121.2 item 2 remainder).
    48	- Locales other than `en-US`.
    49	
    50	## Personas
    51	
    52	See [personas.md](personas.md). Primary: Rosa (Business Reviewer) and Priya (GL Underwriter). Secondary: Noor (Security Administrator, new) and Dana (Platform Engineer).
    53	
    54	## Acceptance Criteria Overview
    55	
    56	Nine stories, 55 acceptance criteria; the per-AC proof map is in [acceptance-criteria-checklist.md](acceptance-criteria-checklist.md).
    57	
    58	- [ ] Tokens never reach the browser: no access, refresh or ID token in cookies readable by script, `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, IndexedDB, URLs or response bodies (S0001, S0009).
    59	- [ ] Every state-changing cookie-authenticated request without a valid CSRF token or with a foreign origin is refused before any engine handler runs (S0002).
    60	- [ ] A burst of concurrent requests after access-token expiry causes exactly one upstream refresh (S0003).
    61	- [ ] A mutation blocked by an expired session is never sent again without the user's explicit re-confirmation, and the re-confirmed request re-checks current revision and authority (S0004, S0009).
    62	- [ ] Logout revokes the refresh token at authentik; an upstream failure is shown to the user and recorded, never reported as success (S0005, S0009).
    63	- [ ] Query caches and in-flight work are cleared on logout, principal change, active knowledge-base switch and grant-revision change (S0005, S0006).
    64	- [ ] A flagged, lazily loaded route adds nothing to the base bundle and is not fetched while its flag is off (S0007).
    65	- [ ] A burst of 1,000 rejected credentials from one client writes at most 21 `authentication_event` rows per 60-second window (S0008).
    66	
    67	## UX / Screens
    68	
    69	| Screen | Purpose | Key Actions |
    70	|--------|---------|-------------|
    71	| Sign-in redirect / callback | Start and complete the OIDC flow; show a sign-in failure without creating a session | Continue to IdP; retry sign-in |
    72	| Shell frame + Home | Show who is signed in, the session state, current memberships and the active knowledge base | Switch active knowledge base; sign out; open a mounted route |
    73	| Session-expired dialog | Re-authenticate without leaving the page; list any blocked action as not submitted | Sign in again (popup); discard and sign out |
    74	| Blocked-action re-confirmation | Ask the user to confirm a mutation that was blocked by session expiry | Re-submit (re-checked); cancel |
    75	| Signed-out page | Confirm sign-out and state whether upstream revocation succeeded | Sign in again |
    76	| Access denied / not found | Explain a denied or unavailable resource without disclosing that it exists | Return home |
    77	| Review Panel (rehosted) | The existing F0001-S0004 proof panel at a session-backed route | Existing panel actions only |
    78	| Too many attempts | Explain throttling after repeated rejected credentials | Wait and retry |
    79	
