   165	## Data Requirements
   166	
   167	**Core Entities:**
   168	- **Browser session** (new, server-side): opaque session identifier (cookie value), stable principal ID, issuer, display name, server-held access/refresh/ID tokens, created-at, last-activity-at, absolute expiry, idle expiry, CSRF secret, active knowledge base, grant revision seen. Storage, encryption at rest and table design are Phase B decisions.
   169	- **Principal / Membership** (existing, F0002): read-only here. Memberships carry tenant, knowledge base, role and grant revision.
   170	- **AuthenticationEvent** (existing, F0001/F0002): gains new reason codes for session and throttling outcomes (`rate_limited`, session expiry and revocation-failure reasons); exact codes are Phase B.
     1	# F0021-S0003 — Renew once and bound session lifetime
     2	
     3	**Story ID:** F0021-S0003
     4	**Feature:** F0021 — Native React semantic shell + OIDC/session contract and safe re-auth behavior
     5	**Title:** Renew once and bound session lifetime
     6	**Priority:** Critical
     7	**Phase:** MVP — v0.1B
     8	**Status:** Not Started
     9	
    10	## User Story
    11	
    12	**As a** business reviewer (Rosa)
    13	**I want** my session renewed quietly on the server while I keep working, and ended by the server when I stop
    14	**So that** I am not interrupted every few minutes, and a session I walked away from cannot be used.
    15	
    16	## Context & Background
    17	
    18	ADR-0051 D1 places renewal on the server; D3 keeps a single coalesced renewal path. §120.5 and §119.5 require timeouts and revocation in the session control plane; an idle-warning modal is UX, not the boundary. Operator decision D1 (2026-11-27): 30-minute idle, 8-hour absolute, warning 2 minutes before idle expiry.
    19	
    20	## Acceptance Criteria
    21	
    22	- [ ] **AC1:** When the server-held access token is expired or within its renewal margin, the next request triggers a server-side refresh-token grant and then proceeds under the renewed token; the browser sees no redirect and no new cookie value other than an unchanged session identifier.
    23	- [ ] **AC2:** For one session, any number of concurrent requests arriving while renewal is needed cause exactly one upstream refresh call; the other requests wait for its result and then proceed (on success) or all receive `401 session_expired` (on failure). This holds across BFF worker processes.
    24	- [ ] **AC3:** When the IdP returns a rotated refresh token, the new one replaces the old one atomically; a renewal that fails (revoked, expired or invalid refresh token, or IdP unavailable after the bounded retry defined in Phase B) ends the session server-side and records the renewal failure in the authentication audit; further requests are rejected with HTTP 401 `session_expired`.
    25	- [ ] **AC4:** A session with no user-initiated request for 30 minutes is ended by the server; background session-status checks do not extend it (PM assumption A5). A request after that gets `401 session_expired` even if the cookie is still present.
    26	- [ ] **AC5:** A session is ended by the server 8 hours after sign-in regardless of activity or successful renewals; continuing requires a full IdP authentication (S0004), never a silent renewal.
    27	- [ ] **AC6:** At 28 minutes of idle time the shell shows a non-blocking warning with a countdown and a "Stay signed in" action that sends one user-initiated request; dismissing or ignoring the warning does not change the server's idle deadline.
    28	
    29	## Edge Cases & Error Scenarios
    30	
    31	Clock skew between BFF and IdP: renewal margin and token expiry checks tolerate skew within the verifier's existing leeway. A renewal racing a logout: logout wins and the renewed tokens are discarded and revoked (S0005). A principal disabled after sign-in: the next request is refused as in F0002 (`unauthenticated`), and the session is ended.
    32	
    33	## Interaction Contract
    34	
    35	Entry: any authenticated request. No user action is needed for renewal. Idle-warning action: "Stay signed in" sends one request; result is the extended idle deadline shown in the status bar. Persistence evidence: session record timestamps (last activity, idle deadline, absolute deadline) observed before and after. Audit: renewal failures and server-ended sessions are recorded (event shape is Phase B).
    36	
    37	## Data Requirements
    38	
    39	Session last-activity, idle deadline, absolute deadline, renewal lock or equivalent; refresh-token rotation timestamp. Exact mechanisms are Phase B decisions.
    40	
    41	## Role-Based Visibility
    42	
    43	Applies to every human session equally; no role-specific timeouts in v0.1.
    44	
    45	## Non-Functional Expectations
    46	
    47	Renewal adds at most one IdP round trip per burst (AC2). Timeouts are configuration values with the D1 defaults. At least 80% changed executable-code coverage in the later feature run.
    48	
    49	## Dependencies
    50	
    51	S0001 (session), S0004 (what the user sees after `session_expired`), S0005 (logout race).
    52	
    53	## Out of Scope
    54	
    55	Role- or tenant-specific timeouts; step-up authentication; device binding.
    56	
    57	## Questions & Assumptions
    58	
    59	No open business-rule question. Operator decision D1 and PM assumption A5 are in the [PRD](PRD.md#risks--assumptions). Renewal margin, lock mechanism and retry bound are Phase B decisions.
    60	
    61	## Definition of Done
    62	
    63	- [ ] Every AC above has a concrete observed proof in the later feature run.
    64	- [ ] A concurrency test with at least 20 parallel requests proving one upstream refresh (AC2), shared with S0009.
    65	- [ ] Time-controlled tests for idle and absolute expiry (AC4, AC5).
    66	- [ ] Documentation and tracker state reflect observed results.
    67	- [ ] Required story-level review provenance is appended to STATUS.md in the feature action.
     1	# F0021-S0005 — Log out with upstream revocation and cache hygiene
     2	
     3	**Story ID:** F0021-S0005
     4	**Feature:** F0021 — Native React semantic shell + OIDC/session contract and safe re-auth behavior
     5	**Title:** Log out with upstream revocation and cache hygiene
     6	**Priority:** Critical
     7	**Phase:** MVP — v0.1B
     8	**Status:** Not Started
     9	
    10	## User Story
    11	
    12	**As a** security administrator (Noor)
    13	**I want** sign-out to revoke the session at the identity provider, end it in Nebula, clear what the browser loaded, and tell the user if revocation failed
    14	**So that** "signed out" is true, and nothing from one user's session is shown to the next.
    15	
    16	## Context & Background
    17	
    18	ADR-0051 D4: logout revokes the server-held refresh token at the IdP and ends the server session; a failure is reported, not hidden by clearing the cookie. D6: query caches and in-flight work are cleared on logout, principal change, tenant switch and relevant grant revision. §119.3 found the CRM revoking a token its browser flow never set.
    19	
    20	## Acceptance Criteria
    21	
    22	- [ ] **AC1:** "Sign out" sends a CSRF-protected request authenticated by the session cookie; the BFF revokes the session's refresh token at authentik's revocation endpoint (RFC 7009), ends the server session, and clears the session cookie (expired `Set-Cookie` with the same attributes).
    23	- [ ] **AC2:** The token revoked is the one the session actually holds after any rotation (S0003 AC3); after logout, a refresh-token grant with that token fails at authentik.
    24	- [ ] **AC3:** If revocation fails (IdP unreachable, non-2xx, timeout), the server session is still ended and its tokens discarded, the failure is recorded durably in the audit log with the principal and reason, and the signed-out page shows the revocation-failed warning. The response never reports success for a failed revocation.
    25	- [ ] **AC4:** After logout, the old session identifier is rejected with HTTP 401 `unauthenticated` for every route, including when replayed from another client.
    26	- [ ] **AC5:** On logout, principal change (S0001 AC7, S0004 AC5), active knowledge-base switch (S0006 AC4) or a change in the principal's grant revision reported by the session endpoint, the shell aborts in-flight requests and clears all query caches and in-memory resource data before rendering anything for the new state.
    27	- [ ] **AC6:** Other open tabs of the same browser show the signed-out state on their next server call and within 60 seconds of the logout (PM assumption A8), without showing data loaded before the logout.
    28	- [ ] **AC7:** After revocation, the BFF ends the user's IdP session through authentik's end-session endpoint, so the next "Sign in" asks for credentials; if that step fails it is reported the same way as AC3.
    29	
    30	## Edge Cases & Error Scenarios
    31	
    32	Logout while a renewal is in flight: logout wins and any newly issued tokens are revoked (S0003). Logout with an already-expired session: cookie cleared, signed-out page shown, no revocation attempted for discarded tokens, and the outcome says so. Double-click on "Sign out": one revocation attempt.
    33	
    34	## Interaction Contract
    35	
    36	Entry: "Sign out" in the shell header or the session-expired dialog's "Discard and sign out". Result: signed-out page with the revocation outcome. Persistence evidence: session record ended; revocation outcome recorded; authentik rejects the revoked refresh token. Audit: a durable record of every logout outcome, including failures (event shape is Phase B).
    37	
    38	## Data Requirements
    39	
    40	Logout outcome record: principal, session reference (not the cookie value), revocation result, end-session result, timestamp. Grant revision exposed by the session endpoint (S0006).
    41	
    42	## Role-Based Visibility
    43	
    44	Every signed-in principal can sign out. No data is shown after logout.
    45	
    46	## Non-Functional Expectations
    47	
    48	Revocation timeout is bounded (Phase B value) so sign-out never hangs. At least 80% changed executable-code coverage in the later feature run.
    49	
    50	## Dependencies
    51	
    52	S0001, S0003, S0006; authentik revocation and end-session endpoints.
    53	
    54	## Out of Scope
    55	
    56	Administrator-initiated session termination screens; back-channel logout from the IdP (later hardening, F0026).
    57	
    58	## Questions & Assumptions
    59	
    60	No open business-rule question. PM assumption A8 is in the [PRD](PRD.md#risks--assumptions). The cross-tab signal mechanism and grant-revision polling interval are Phase B decisions.
    61	
    62	## Definition of Done
    63	
    64	- [ ] Every AC above has a concrete observed proof in the later feature run.
    65	- [ ] Forced upstream-failure test for AC3 (shared with S0009).
    66	- [ ] Cache-clearing tests for each AC5 trigger.
    67	- [ ] Documentation and tracker state reflect observed results.
    68	- [ ] Required story-level review provenance is appended to STATUS.md in the feature action.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:18:ADR-0051 chose a same-origin backend-for-frontend (BFF) with an opaque cookie, server-held tokens, CSRF and origin checks, coalesced renewal, upstream revocation and cache hygiene. It is accepted only when master blueprint section 121.2 items 8 and 9 pass against the real flow. F0021 Phase A (nine stories, 55 ACs) fixed the business rules: 30-minute idle and 8-hour absolute limits (D1), the shell scope with the rehosted Review Panel (D2), popup re-authentication with explicit re-confirmation (D3), and 20 rejected credentials per client per 60 seconds (D4). The engine today has one credential path: a bearer token verified by `OidcJwksVerifier`, resolved by the F0002 `PrincipalResolver`, with rejections written to `authentication_event`. The authentik dev provider `brain` is a public client, and the experience app is a proof page that takes a token in its URL.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:25:- One public origin serves the shell at `/` and the API under `/api/`. The front strips `/api` before the engine: the Vite dev server and `vite preview` proxy locally; the production ingress is F0026. Engine routes keep their current paths (`/reviews/*`, `/content/*`, `/facts/*`, `/health`). New BFF routes: `GET /auth/login`, `GET /auth/callback`, `POST /auth/logout`, `GET /session`, `PUT /session/active-knowledge-base`.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:38:- `browser_session`: session reference (UUID, never the cookie), cookie digest (unique SHA-256 of the cookie secret), principal, issuer and subject, display name, created, last activity, idle and absolute deadlines, access-token expiry, encrypted token bundle and key ID, renewal count, CSRF digest, active tenant and knowledge base (composite FK to `knowledge_base(id, tenant_id)`), ended timestamp and end reason.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:39:- `session_event` (append-only, same trigger pattern as migration 0007): session created, replaced, renewed, renewal failed, ended (idle, absolute, principal change, principal disabled), logout with revocation and end-session outcomes, active knowledge-base change.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:47:- Login-binding cookie `__Host-nebula_login`: same attributes, `Max-Age=600`; its digest is stored on the login attempt and must match at the callback (login CSRF and fixation defence). It is cleared at the callback.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:48:- `SameSite=Lax`, not `Strict`: the callback is a top-level navigation from authentik, and `Strict` drops the binding cookie there and the session cookie on the first navigation after it. CSRF is enforced by D5, not by `SameSite`.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:51:### D5. Cookie request path and CSRF
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:58:4. Unsafe methods (`POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`): reject with `403 csrf_rejected` when `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`; when `Origin` is present and is not `BRAIN_PUBLIC_ORIGIN`; when `Origin` is absent and the `Referer` origin is missing or different; or when `X-CSRF-Token` is missing or its SHA-256 differs from the session's digest (constant-time). The cause goes to `authentication_event` (`csrf_rejected`). No handler or write runs.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:63:The CSRF token is 256 random bits per session, created with the session, returned only in the `GET /session` body and held in page memory. A new session (sign-in or re-authentication) gets a new token. Responses to cookie requests and all `/auth` and `/session` responses carry `Cache-Control: no-store` and `Vary: Cookie`; no CORS headers are added.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:65:Stable outcomes: `401 unauthenticated`, `401 session_expired`, `403 csrf_rejected`, `400 ambiguous_credentials`, `429 rate_limited`, and the engine's existing non-disclosing `404` for denials. New `AuthenticationReason` values: `session_unknown`, `session_expired`, `renewal_failed`, `principal_mismatch`, `state_invalid`, `binding_mismatch`, `nonce_mismatch`, `idp_error`, `code_exchange_failed`, `csrf_rejected`, `ambiguous_credentials`, `rate_limited`.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:73:- Logout takes the same lock, so logout and renewal serialize: a renewal that finds the session ended stops; a logout after a renewal revokes the rotated token.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:77:- `POST /auth/logout` (D5 checks; an ended session's CSRF digest still validates). Under the row lock: end the session (`logout`), revoke the current refresh token at the revocation endpoint (RFC 7009, `token_type_hint=refresh_token`, client authentication, 5 s timeout, no retry), set the token ciphertext to NULL, record `logout` with the outcome, and clear the cookie.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:78:- Response `logout-result-v1`: `revocation` = `succeeded` | `failed` (with a non-secret reason) | `not_attempted` (no live tokens), plus `end_session_url`, or `null` with `end_session` = `unavailable` when discovery has no end-session endpoint. Revocation failure is never reported as success.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:79:- The end-session URL carries `client_id`, `post_logout_redirect_uri` (`/signed-out`) and `state`, and **no `id_token_hint`**, so no token appears in a URL. The shell keeps the outcome in `sessionStorage` under `nebula.signout` (outcome only, no token), then navigates top-level to the URL. The signed-out page reads and deletes it.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:92:- Each rejected credential (bearer rejection, unknown or ended session cookie, callback failure) runs `INSERT … ON CONFLICT (client_key, window_start) DO UPDATE SET rejected_count = rejected_count + 1 RETURNING rejected_count`, which is atomic across workers. Count ≤ 20: today's response and event. Count = 21: one `rate_limited` event, then `429`. Count > 21: `429 rate_limited` with `Retry-After` (seconds to window end), no event. Bound: 21 rows per client per window.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:97:- `GET /session` returns `browser-session-v1`: principal (ID, display name, kind, issuer), session deadlines and server time, CSRF token, current memberships with tenant and knowledge-base display names and role, `grant_revision`, active knowledge base, and flags. `grant_revision` is an opaque digest of the sorted current memberships (ID, grant revision); any grant, revocation or revision change changes it. It returns no token.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:109:- One `apiClient` wrapper is the only `fetch` caller. It uses `credentials: "same-origin"`, adds `X-CSRF-Token` on unsafe methods, registers each request with the hygiene abort registry, maps the D5 outcomes, never sets `Authorization`, and never retries an unsafe method. ESLint rules forbid `localStorage`, `indexedDB`, `caches`, and `sessionStorage` outside the sign-out outcome key.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:110:- Hygiene triggers (logout, principal change, active knowledge-base change, `grant_revision` change) abort every registered request, call `queryClient.clear()`, reset resource stores, and only then render the new state.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:130:- **`SameSite=Strict`:** breaks the IdP callback and the first post-login navigation. Rejected; CSRF is enforced by D5.
planning-mds/architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md:132:- **CSRF double-submit cookie:** needs a script-readable cookie. Rejected in favour of a synchronizer token in the session body.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0002-protect-cookie-authenticated-calls-with-csrf-and-origin-checks.md:1:# F0021-S0002 — Protect cookie-authenticated calls with CSRF and origin checks
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0002-protect-cookie-authenticated-calls-with-csrf-and-origin-checks.md:5:**Title:** Protect cookie-authenticated calls with CSRF and origin checks
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0002-protect-cookie-authenticated-calls-with-csrf-and-origin-checks.md:18:ADR-0051 D2 requires CSRF and origin checks on every state-changing cookie-authenticated request. D3 keeps distinct outcomes for unauthenticated, expired-recoverable and denied requests. §120.5: UI guards are convenience only and the backend rejects direct requests; resource existence must not leak where policy requires. ADR-0049's verify-before-read ordering stays.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0002-protect-cookie-authenticated-calls-with-csrf-and-origin-checks.md:23:- [ ] **AC2:** A state-changing request (`POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`) authenticated by the session cookie is rejected with HTTP 403 and a stable `csrf_rejected` problem code, before any route handler or storage write runs (the rejection and its cause are recorded in the security audit log), when the CSRF token is missing or does not match the session, or when `Origin` (or `Referer` when `Origin` is absent) is not the shell's own origin, or `Sec-Fetch-Site` is `cross-site`.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0002-protect-cookie-authenticated-calls-with-csrf-and-origin-checks.md:24:- [ ] **AC3:** Safe methods (`GET`, `HEAD`) never change state and are not CSRF-checked; a cookie-authenticated `GET` from a cross-site context is still answered under normal authorization and the response cannot be read cross-origin (no permissive CORS headers are added).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0002-protect-cookie-authenticated-calls-with-csrf-and-origin-checks.md:31:A CSRF token from an earlier session is rejected after re-authentication (tokens are bound to the session). A login-CSRF attempt (attacker-initiated callback) fails S0001 AC4 because the state is not the browser's own. A missing `Origin` and `Referer` on a state-changing request is refused.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0002-protect-cookie-authenticated-calls-with-csrf-and-origin-checks.md:35:Entry: any shell screen calling the engine. Read requests carry the cookie; state-changing requests also carry the CSRF token the shell obtains from the session endpoint. Refusal result: a problem-details response the shell maps to sign-in, the session-expired dialog, an in-context denied message, or not-found. No editable state. Audit: the existing authorization decision audit for engine routes; CSRF refusals are recorded (event shape is Phase B).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0002-protect-cookie-authenticated-calls-with-csrf-and-origin-checks.md:39:Per-session CSRF secret; the shell's allowed origin as configuration. Token format and delivery are Phase B decisions.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0008-throttle-rejected-credentials.md:26:- [ ] **AC5:** The rule applies equally to bearer-API requests, cookie-authenticated requests with an unknown or ended session, and sign-in callback failures (S0001 AC4). The client address is the immediate peer, or a forwarded address only from a configured trusted proxy (PM assumption A6).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/contract-inventory.yaml:48:- name: logout-result-v1
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/contract-inventory.yaml:50:  id: https://nebula.local/schemas/logout-result-v1.schema.json
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/contract-inventory.yaml:51:  source: planning-mds/schemas/logout-result-v1.schema.json
