planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/PRD.md:18:- **Metric:** master blueprint §121.2 items 8 (session transport) and 9 (mutation continuity) pass against the real authentik issuance, storage, renewal and logout flow, including an upstream revocation failure. These are ADR-0051's formal acceptance conditions.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/PRD.md:19:- **Baseline:** today the proof-scope Review Panel (F0001-S0004) takes a bearer token from the URL or a text field. No session, renewal, logout, CSRF protection or shell exists.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/PRD.md:24:- **Current State:** the only UI is a proof page that asks for a raw bearer token. The CRM reference mixes an HttpOnly-cookie model with browser-direct renewal that writes tokens to `sessionStorage`, and its logout revokes a refresh token the browser never set (§119.3). Since F0002, every rejected credential writes one durable `authentication_event` row with no edge throttle (F0002 security review, medium).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/PRD.md:32:- Cookie-authenticated calls to the existing engine routes with CSRF and origin checks on every state-changing request, and distinct unauthenticated / session-expired / denied / not-found outcomes (S0002).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/PRD.md:35:- Logout that revokes the server-held refresh token upstream, ends the server session and reports an upstream failure; cache and in-flight-work clearing on logout, principal change, active knowledge-base switch and grant-revision change (S0005).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/PRD.md:59:- [ ] Every state-changing cookie-authenticated request without a valid CSRF token or with a foreign origin is refused before any engine handler runs (S0002).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/PRD.md:63:- [ ] Query caches and in-flight work are cleared on logout, principal change, active knowledge-base switch and grant-revision change (S0005, S0006).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/PRD.md:168:- **Browser session** (new, server-side): opaque session identifier (cookie value), stable principal ID, issuer, display name, server-held access/refresh/ID tokens, created-at, last-activity-at, absolute expiry, idle expiry, CSRF secret, active knowledge base, grant revision seen. Storage, encryption at rest and table design are Phase B decisions.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/PRD.md:217:- **A8 — Other tabs:** after logout or session end in one tab, other tabs of the same browser show the signed-out state on their next server call and within 60 seconds.
