planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0005-log-out-with-upstream-revocation-and-cache-hygiene.md:18:ADR-0051 D4: logout revokes the server-held refresh token at the IdP and ends the server session; a failure is reported, not hidden by clearing the cookie. D6: query caches and in-flight work are cleared on logout, principal change, tenant switch and relevant grant revision. §119.3 found the CRM revoking a token its browser flow never set.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0005-log-out-with-upstream-revocation-and-cache-hygiene.md:22:- [ ] **AC1:** "Sign out" sends a CSRF-protected request authenticated by the session cookie; the BFF revokes the session's refresh token at authentik's revocation endpoint (RFC 7009), ends the server session, and clears the session cookie (expired `Set-Cookie` with the same attributes).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0005-log-out-with-upstream-revocation-and-cache-hygiene.md:23:- [ ] **AC2:** The token revoked is the one the session actually holds after any rotation (S0003 AC3); after logout, a refresh-token grant with that token fails at authentik.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0005-log-out-with-upstream-revocation-and-cache-hygiene.md:25:- [ ] **AC4:** After logout, the old session identifier is rejected with HTTP 401 `unauthenticated` for every route, including when replayed from another client.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0005-log-out-with-upstream-revocation-and-cache-hygiene.md:26:- [ ] **AC5:** On logout, principal change (S0001 AC7, S0004 AC5), active knowledge-base switch (S0006 AC4) or a change in the principal's grant revision reported by the session endpoint, the shell aborts in-flight requests and clears all query caches and in-memory resource data before rendering anything for the new state.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0005-log-out-with-upstream-revocation-and-cache-hygiene.md:27:- [ ] **AC6:** Other open tabs of the same browser show the signed-out state on their next server call and within 60 seconds of the logout (PM assumption A8), without showing data loaded before the logout.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0005-log-out-with-upstream-revocation-and-cache-hygiene.md:32:Logout while a renewal is in flight: logout wins and any newly issued tokens are revoked (S0003). Logout with an already-expired session: cookie cleared, signed-out page shown, no revocation attempted for discarded tokens, and the outcome says so. Double-click on "Sign out": one revocation attempt.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0005-log-out-with-upstream-revocation-and-cache-hygiene.md:36:Entry: "Sign out" in the shell header or the session-expired dialog's "Discard and sign out". Result: signed-out page with the revocation outcome. Persistence evidence: session record ended; revocation outcome recorded; authentik rejects the revoked refresh token. Audit: a durable record of every logout outcome, including failures (event shape is Phase B).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0005-log-out-with-upstream-revocation-and-cache-hygiene.md:44:Every signed-in principal can sign out. No data is shown after logout.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0005-log-out-with-upstream-revocation-and-cache-hygiene.md:56:Administrator-initiated session termination screens; back-channel logout from the IdP (later hardening, F0026).
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/feature-assembly-plan.md:12:Add a backend-for-frontend (BFF) to the engine API process. It handles sign-in, the session cookie, CSRF and origin checks, coalesced renewal, logout with upstream revocation, a session endpoint, and a rejected-credential throttle.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/feature-assembly-plan.md:29:- Three design schemas under `planning-mds/schemas/`: `browser-session-v1`, `active-knowledge-base-update-v1` and `logout-result-v1`.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/feature-assembly-plan.md:35:| R1 | **S0002 AC4 says "an authorization denial → `403`".** No engine route returns 403 for a denial. Every denial is the non-disclosing 404 (`brain-api.yaml` `Forbidden`: "user denials are reported as 404"; master blueprint section 118.2). | The design keeps the engine unchanged. 403 is used only for `csrf_rejected`, and a denial stays the existing 404 with the session kept (never 401). The AC4 proof shows each outcome is distinct and the session survives a denial. **Proposed PM wording correction at feature G0:** "an authorization denial → the engine's existing non-disclosing `404`, with the session kept". Confirmed by the operator with `approve-phase-b` (2026-11-27). |
