planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0004-re-authenticate-without-losing-work-or-replaying-mutations.md:25:- [ ] **AC4:** A re-confirmed request is a new request: it carries the new session's CSRF token and the engine re-checks current authority and current resource revision; a stale item or a lost grant is rejected with the engine's existing denied or not found response, which the shell shows in context without retrying; the engine's existing audit records the re-confirmed request like any other.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0009-prove-session-transport-and-mutation-continuity.md:18:ADR-0051's formal acceptance needs master blueprint §121.2 items 8 (session transport) and 9 (mutation continuity) to pass against the real issuance, storage, renewal and logout flow, including an upstream revocation failure. §119.3: test logout with actual issuance, storage and renewal, not only a cookie-clear response. ADR-0049 leaves items 8 and 9 open for F0021.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0009-prove-session-transport-and-mutation-continuity.md:22:- [ ] **AC1:** An end-to-end suite runs a real browser against the local stack (authentik from the dev blueprint, PostgreSQL, engine, BFF, built shell) and, after sign-in, renewal and logout, inspects cookies, `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, IndexedDB, Cache Storage, URLs and response bodies: no access, refresh or ID token appears, and the session cookie has the S0001 AC2 attributes.
planning-mds/features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/F0021-S0009-prove-session-transport-and-mutation-continuity.md:23:- [ ] **AC2:** The suite forces access-token expiry and fires at least 20 parallel requests; authentik observes exactly one refresh grant for the session, and the rotated refresh token is the one later revoked at logout.
